    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27622" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magnātus</span></b> , i,
		m., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magnas</span></b> ,
			ātis, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				great man, important person, magnate</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnes magnates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Judith, 5, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in conspectu magnatorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Sir. 38, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">33, 19</span></i>; Inscr. ap. Demster. ad Rosini Antiq. 2,
			12: magnates, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγιστᾶνες</span>,
		Gloss.</div>
